      "type": "mini_coding",
      "title": "Print the delivery label from a typed order",
      "description": "Every bag that leaves the Chợ Sớm packing hub carries a label printed from a DeliveryOrder. Many of its properties are optional: the apartment, floor and building, the second phone number, the cash to collect, the note. Write formatLabel, which returns the label lines (slot and FRAGILE, recipient, street line from the parts that exist, ward line, cash to collect or paid online, trimmed note), and formatVnd, which puts a dot between every group of three digits. Optional properties must never print as \"undefined\", and 0 is a real floor. The test runner reads a JSON array of orders and prints the labels separated by ---.",
